Idempotent, self-contained script to compute non-KMX charge-off timing per account.

This module mirrors the logic in :py:mod:`acariskandpricing.nonkmx_roa.mroa` for non-KMX
scenarios (``get_scenario_timing`` and ``get_scenario_timing_frn_4``) but embeds the necessary
lookup tables and constants as pure Python dicts to ensure deterministic behavior without
external data file dependencies.

Usage::

    python notebooks/nonkmx_chargeoff_timing.py

Output: Prints CSV to stdout with columns: ``acct_num,charge_off_month``

The script computes charge-off timing for every account in the provided input list
and outputs results deterministically based on:
- Loan term (in months)
- Line of business (LOB)
- Model score or model score tag (depending on model version)
- Model version (franchise3.1, franchise4.0, franchise4.1, etc.)

All heuristics and lookup tables are hard-coded; no network or external dependencies.
"""
